# cheap-mem local state (only appears in a user's memory clone, not this repo)
.mem/inbox-seen.json
.mem/inbox-whoami
.mem/watch.log
.mem/watch.lock
.mem/reflect-marker/

# A memory accidentally created inside the package. `mem init` writes
# these into whatever directory it is pointed at; running it here by
# mistake must not put someone's memory skeleton into the tool.
/.mem/
/FACTS.md
/global/
/projects/
/inbox/
/raw/

# Store: the BYTES stay out, the register stays in.
# The audit trail is store/register.jsonl (hash, size, type, origin,
# purpose) — small, readable, redactable. The objects themselves do not
# belong in a history that never forgets: the clone would grow without
# bound, and deleted content could never actually be removed (GDPR
# Art. 17). Bytes gone, register line kept as a tombstone — that is the
# deletion that works.
store/objects/

# Raw captures live in the archive, not the repo (src/archive.mjs).
# Default location; another one is named by CHEAP_MEM_ARCHIVE.
.mem/raw/

# Coverage-Berichte
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Runtime state of ONE clone. It describes this container and nothing
# else, so it must never travel — a number from here carried to another
# machine is invented. The clone mark lives here too: if it travelled,
# two clones would produce an add/add conflict on the mark instead of
# on the messages, which is the same outage under a new name.
.pipeline/

# The one deliberate exception. This baseline records the byte size of
# files that are COMMITTED, so it is a fact about the repository, not
# about a container — it is the reference point the shrink check
# compares against, and it has to be the same for everyone.
!.pipeline/shrink-baseline.json

# cheap-mem: derived state and secrets
# API keys. NEVER commit this.
.mem/embed.env
# Local rollback watermark. Never commit: a tracked one
# travels back with the checkout it is meant to detect.
.mem/epoch.json
# derived: rebuilt in milliseconds. Since B8 (2026-09-20, see
# src/indexcache.mjs) the live cache is the DIRECTORY below, not this
# file — an old single-file cache from before that change may still be
# lying around on a machine that has not rebuilt yet, so it stays listed
# too. Checked before adding the directory line: `/.mem/` above already
# blanket-ignores everything under `.mem/` IN THIS REPO, so neither line
# in this whole "derived state" block actually needs to match anything
# here — they are kept as the readable enumeration of what a real
# memory's `.gitignore` (written by `mem init`, `src/cli/githook.mjs`)
# has to cover, not because this repo's own ignore rules depend on them.
.mem/search-index.json
.mem/search-index/
# derived: rebuild with `mem embed backfill`
.mem/vectors.db
# per-machine read positions
.mem/raw-offsets.json
# transient
.mem/digest-bell.json
# transient
.mem/digest.lock
# local log
.mem/digest.log
# generated by `mem hooks install`, machine-specific
.mem/hooks/
# per-machine observation ledger — retrieval/ranking never reads it
.pipeline/observations.jsonl

# Atlas runs. Each `npm run atlas` writes a timestamped directory; those are
# working output, not history. The ONE committed artefact is
# bench/atlas-baseline.json — the run a later run compares itself against.
# Committing every run would make the diff of this repo unreadable and would
# also bake a particular machine's timings into the history as if they were
# a property of the code.
bench/atlas-out/
